    "highlights": [
      "Natural gas costs more here than in most states ($2.49 per therm, the 2nd highest), so gas's running-cost advantage is smaller than the national picture suggests.",
      "88% of Florida homes heat water with electricity, against 46% nationally, so most replacements here are electric-to-electric and need no gas or vent work.",
      "Incoming water stays near 69.3 °F even in the coldest month, so a single whole-house tankless unit can run 2 full-flow showers at once all year.",
      "Where you live inside Florida matters: the same 50-gallon gas job is about $1,938 in the Miami-Fort Lauderdale-West Palm Beach, FL area and $1,805 in the Jacksonville, FL area."
